 many frontier discs that the opponent can exploit.\n\nReason: Since all options are symmetric and result in a mathematically identical board state (under rotation or reflection), there is no strategic disadvantage to any choice. (F, 5) is chosen as it is a standard, conventional opening move in Reversi/Othello, effectively contesting the center.\n\nAnswer: (F, 5)"}
